    feat: MCP bridge, RAG index fixes, and asset-edit/batch UX
    
    MCP
    - New loopback control bridge (src/main/bridge) exposing the app's existing IPC
      commands over 127.0.0.1:8765, captured by wrapping ipcMain.handle so the
      renderer path is untouched and both transports run the same functions.
      Allowlisted to library read/write; project, dialog, settings, Blender and
      shell commands are deliberately excluded.
    - New mcp/zeuspack-mcp stdio server + .mcp.json, so Claude can browse, search
      (keyword + semantic) and read/write asset metadata in a running instance.
    
    RAG indexing
    - Derive point ids from the asset's json_path instead of the SQLite
      autoincrement id: rescans reassign those ids, which orphaned every vector.
      Stable ids mean re-embedding upserts over the same point.
    - Scope index and search by pack_id, and clear a pack's vectors before a
      re-embed so stale points can't pile up beside the new ones.
    - Tagger: protect FileName/Category from AI overwrite — those are system
      managed (folder layout + categories JSON).
    
    Asset edit modal
    - Pause the background DB sync while the modal is open; a silent refresh
      mid-edit reverted unsaved changes (e.g. the category dropdown).
    - Enter saves — skips textareas, modifier combos, IME composition, and the
      category dropdown.
    - Category dropdown is now type-to-search, with prefix-first ranking and
      arrow-key navigation.
    
    Batch tagger
    - Leaving batch mode no longer tears down a running batch: the tray, progress
      and results survive, so assets can be edited while tagging finishes.
    - Add a collapse toggle; ✕/Stop now discards explicitly, and runs are abortable
      via a run token so a discarded loop stops writing to the store.

